import MathEconLib.Choice.Conditions.General.IrrelevanceOfRejectedAlternatives

/-!
# Irrelevance of rejected contracts

`ChoiceFunction.Consistent` is the set-form consistency condition for general
choice: removing rejected alternatives does not change the choice. When the
alternatives are contracts, it is called irrelevance of rejected contracts
(IRC).

This topic entrypoint imports the canonical definition and its idempotence
lemma from
`MathEconLib.Choice.Conditions.General.IrrelevanceOfRejectedAlternatives`.
The contracts terminology does not introduce a separate predicate or impose
any matching-market structure.
-/
